{"availability":"available","full":"Bigda7/jobradar-frontend","name":"jobradar-frontend","description":"React and TypeScript dashboard for ranked job discovery, source monitoring, and application tracking, deployed through a secure server-side API proxy.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-25T14:56:25Z","updated":"2026-10-05T17:04:35Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://jobradar-frontend-pink.vercel.app","topics":["dnd-kit","github-actions","job-search","job-tracker","react","tailwindcss","tanstack-query","typescript","vercel","vite","zod"],"demo":"https://stats.uptimerobot.com/pbYg91DSyR","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:07.948Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:07.948Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:07.948Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T15:46:07.948Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Production React client for JobRadar, a self-hosted job intelligence platform that collects remote opportunities, scores them against a deterministic profile, and turns the results into an actionable application workflow.","The interface combines ranked matches, a searchable job catalog, source monitoring, and a device-local Kanban tracker. It uses strict runtime validation at API and storage boundaries, route-level code splitting, accessible UI primitives, and a security-focused deployment configuration.","The deployed application is intentionally public as a portfolio demonstration. Visitors can view the job catalog, match scores and reasons, and source health metrics. The tracker belongs to each visitor's current browser and is not shared with the backend. Detailed source errors and backend credentials are not part of the public API response."],"features":["Matches feed — Browse deterministically scored opportunities grouped into Top (85–100), Strong (70–84), Good (55–69), and Below Target tiers. Switch between board and compact list views, sort the loaded page, and…","Job catalog — Search the stored catalog with a debounced query, work mode, employment type, monthly salary in a selected currency, and pagination controls.","Source monitoring — Review each configured source, its enabled state, last run, last successful run, and issue status without exposing internal diagnostics.","Application tracker — Manage a local Kanban pipeline: Saved -> Applied -> Interview -> Offer, with a separate archive, drag-and-drop movement, accessible status controls, job snapshots, autosaved notes, and cross-tab…","Command palette — Use Cmd+K on macOS or Ctrl+/ on Windows and Linux to navigate between sections, search loaded matches, and query remote jobs."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Bigda7/jobradar-frontend/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"046f6bf2157c40faf4589606a7c2398c8d24e17f3aa78f762eeb5c0479d369ac","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:08.046Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:08.046Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Production React client for JobRadar, a self-hosted job intelligence platform that collects remote opportunities, scores them against a deterministic profile, and turns the results into an actionable application workflow.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Bigda7/jobradar-frontend/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"046f6bf2157c40faf4589606a7c2398c8d24e17f3aa78f762eeb5c0479d369ac","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Bigda7/jobradar-frontend/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:08.046Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-05T17:04:35Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Bigda7/jobradar-frontend/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:08.047Z","hash":"046f6bf2157c40faf4589606a7c2398c8d24e17f3aa78f762eeb5c0479d369ac","originalBytes":10978,"storedBytes":10978,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["api","run","source","local","npm","jobradar","production","tok